In article <11270@etana.tut.fi> ma62141@uikku.tut.fi (Antila Marko) writes:
> Has Hawaiian T-shirt any use whatsoever?

Anything in hack is useful, if you're creative enough!
But some things are more useful than others.
A Hawaiian Shirt is armor, just like plate mail, and anything that
affects armor affects it.  Scrolls of enchant or destroy armor,
curses that make it non-removable, another piece of armor for a
nymph to steal instead of your +6 crystal plate mail.

Remember that each item can be enchanted only a certain amount;
the shirt gives you one more thing to wear if you have lots of
enchant-armor scrolls.  A Hawaiian shirt also tells shopkeepers that
you're the kind of rich stupid person who might pay more money for 
some worthless junk.

